 category, requirements

- Upload images, videos, audio and briefs; name each @handle and map it to a
  use (character, product, backdrop, prop, style, logo, motion, footage,
  voice, music, voiceover, sfx, brief). AI description + suggested use on
  upload; audio asks how it should be used.
- Script writer receives uploads and product requirements as data; roles and
  scenes carry referenceId / referenceIds; requirement checklist on review.
- Ad genres (slice of life, problem-solution, customer story, ...) plus a
  custom tone.
- Per-story 'is this medical or CA-related?' question: only those get NMC /
  ICAI rules and a banned-words list; regulated brands keep their rules.
- Upload images attach as Wan references; footage, music, voiceover and SFX
  are mixed locally after render with hash checks.

